---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../components/HeroSection.astro';
import KeyMetrics from '../components/KeyMetrics.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const events = (await getCollection('labLog')).filter((e) => !e.data.draft).sort((a,b) => b.data.date.valueOf()-a.data.date.valueOf()).slice(0,4);
const labels = { measured:'MEASURED', 'active-experiment':'ACTIVE EXPERIMENT', 'instrument-validation':'INSTRUMENT / VALIDATION', 'programme-bet':'PROGRAMME BET', foundation:'COMPLETED INFRASTRUCTURE' };
---
<BaseLayout title="Failure-First — We break AI systems and keep the receipts" description="Embodied and agentic AI experiments: watch failures acquire consequences, follow the causal chain, and inspect what the evidence actually earns.">
  <HeroSection title="A Go2 started prone.<br /><em>Did it actually stand?</em>" subtitle="The apparatus checked the body-height transition. No model entered this control trace — and the receipt says so." animation="cascade">
    <!-- CORRECTED 2026-08-23 (docs/audits/EVIDENCE_PROMOTION_AUDIT_2026-08-23.md):
         primary CTA now opens the SimLab front door (the curated FEATURED
         shortlist) instead of dropping cold visitors straight into the single
         vendor-stand evidence preset. The evidence preset remains one click
         away via the secondary link, demoted not deleted. -->
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="primary-cta" href="https://sim.failurefirst.ai/">Enter SimLab &rarr;</a><a class="secondary-cta" href="https://sim.failurefirst.ai/?preset=evidence">Inspect the measured control</a><a class="secondary-cta" href="/lab-log/">See the stranger experiments</a></div>
  </HeroSection>

  <section class="phenomenon scroll-reveal">
    <p class="kicker">PHENOMENON EARNS ATTENTION.</p>
    <h2>The live questions start when words, peers, and bodies share one causal chain.</h2>
    <p class="lead">In the experiments now being built and run, a model receives a message, its belief about the world may change, and a peer may carry the change further. Then a robot moves, fails to recover, or does nothing at all. Those experiments stay labelled active until matched receipts exist. The control above demonstrates the physical trace apparatus, not model cognition.</p>
    <div class="causal-chain" aria-label="Failure-First research loop"><span>SENSE</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>ASSIMILATE</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>NORMALISE</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>TEST</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>MUTATE</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>EMBODY</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>FALSIFY</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>RECEIPT</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>PUBLISH</span></div>
    <p><a href="/simviz/">Watch the trace</a> &rarr; see why we think it happened &rarr; see what would kill that explanation &rarr; inspect the receipt.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="now scroll-reveal">
    <div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">NOW / LAB LOG</p><h2>Things that happened in the machine</h2></div><a href="/lab-log/">Full log &rarr;</a></div>
    <div class="event-list">{events.map((event) => <article class="event"><div class="event-meta"><time datetime={event.data.date.toISOString()}>{event.data.date.toLocaleDateString('en-AU',{day:'numeric',month:'short'})}</time><span class={`status status--${event.data.status}`}>{labels[event.data.status]}</span><span>{event.data.specimen}</span></div><h3>{event.data.title}</h3><p>{event.data.summary}</p><a href={`/lab-log/#${event.id}`}>Open event &rarr;</a></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="specimens scroll-reveal">
    <p class="kicker">CURRENT SPECIMENS</p><h2>Questions with their status left attached</h2>
    <div class="specimen-grid">
      <article class="specimen-card"><span class="status status--active-experiment">ACTIVE EXPERIMENT</span><h3>BAD APPLE / ARMOURER</h3><p class="question">Does accumulated jailbreak knowledge make RED better at changing another embodied agent's behaviour?</p><p>Apparatus ready. Matched A1/A2 run pending. <strong>No scientific verdict.</strong></p><a href="/lab-log/#2026-08-22-bad-apple-armourer">Follow the experiment &rarr;</a></article>
      <article class="specimen-card"><span class="status status--active-experiment">ACTIVE EXPERIMENT · AS OF 00:08 UTC</span><h3>OBLITERATUS / Qwen3.8-27B</h3><p class="question">Can we remove refusal without removing the interesting parts of the model's mind?</p><p>Baseline banked; pinned surgery retry active at the recorded update. <strong>No candidate result.</strong></p><a href="/lab-log/#2026-08-23-obliteratus-qwen">Follow the operation &rarr;</a></article>
      <article class="specimen-card"><span class="status status--instrument-validation">INSTRUMENT / VALIDATION</span><h3>LulzBench</h3><p class="question">Does a model still get the joke after its safety circuitry changes?</p><p>320 matched funny/bare controls. L2 semantic audit complete; human calibration pending. <strong>Not human-validated.</strong></p><a href="/lab-log/#2026-08-22-lulzbench-controls">Inspect the instrument &rarr;</a></article>
      <article class="specimen-card"><span class="status status--foundation">COMPLETED INFRASTRUCTURE</span><h3>ASSIMILATOR</h3><p class="question">Can outside adversarial knowledge become reusable without losing provenance?</p><p>Eight technique objects compiled into a deterministic, content-addressed handbook and consumed by BAD APPLE. Infrastructure, not a result.</p><a href="/lab-log/#2026-08-22-assimilator-handbook">Inspect the organ &rarr;</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="trust scroll-reveal">
    <p class="kicker">APPARATUS EARNS TRUST.</p><h2>The corpus is why the claims are believable. It is not the whole identity.</h2>
    <p>Matched controls, baseline refusals, frozen prompts, exact model outputs, physics traces, hostile graders, falsifiers, hashes, and nulls keep an interesting event from becoming a story we merely liked.</p>
    <KeyMetrics />
    <div class="trust-links"><a href="/results/">Measured results</a><a href="/research/methodology/">How claims are graded</a><a href="https://github.com/failurefirst/failure-first">Code and public receipts</a></div>
    <p class="caveat">We do not certify systems as safe. We document where they fail, what changed, whether the consequence survives a matched test, and what would falsify our explanation.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="streams scroll-reveal"><h2>Choose the aperture</h2><div class="stream-grid"><a href="/simviz/"><strong>SimLab</strong><span>Experience the evidence.</span></a><a href="/lab-log/"><strong>Lab Log</strong><span>What just happened.</span></a><a href="/blog/"><strong>Blog</strong><span>Readable autopsies.</span></a><a href="/daily-paper/"><strong>Daily Paper</strong><span>What entered from outside.</span></a><a href="/research/reports/"><strong>Reports</strong><span>Full argument and method.</span></a><a href="/services/"><strong>Services</strong><span>Put a bounded real system in the apparatus.</span></a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .hero-actions{display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1.5rem}.primary-cta,.secondary-cta{display:inline-block;padding:.75rem 1rem;border:1px solid var(--accent-primary);border-radius:4px;font-weight:700}.primary-cta{background:var(--accent-primary);color:var(--bg)}.secondary-cta{color:var(--accent-primary)}
  .kicker,.event-meta,.status{font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase}.kicker{color:var(--accent-primary);margin-bottom:.5rem}.phenomenon,.trust{max-width:760px}.lead{font-size:1.2rem}.causal-chain{display:flex;gap:.55rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:1.5rem 0;color:var(--fg-dim)}.causal-chain span{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem .5rem;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:.75rem}.causal-chain b{color:var(--accent-primary)}
  .section-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;align-items:end}.event-list{border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.event{padding:1.5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.event-meta{display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap;color:var(--fg-muted)}.event h3{font-size:1.35rem;margin:.6rem 0}.event p{max-width:760px}.status{display:inline-block;width:max-content;color:var(--accent-primary)}.status--active-experiment{color:var(--status-active-experiment)}.status--instrument-validation{color:var(--status-instrument-validation)}.status--programme-bet{color:var(--status-programme-bet)}.status--foundation{color:var(--status-foundation)}.status--measured{color:var(--status-measured)}
  .specimen-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:1rem}.specimen-card{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--bg-card)}.specimen-card h3{margin:.75rem 0}.specimen-card .question{font-size:1.08rem;color:var(--fg)}
  .trust-links{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:1.25rem 0}.caveat{border-left:2px solid var(--accent-primary);padding-left:1rem;color:var(--fg-dim)}.stream-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--border)}.stream-grid a{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.35rem;padding:1.25rem;background:var(--bg);border:0}.stream-grid span{color:var(--fg-dim)}
  @media(max-width:700px){.specimen-grid,.stream-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.section-head{align-items:start;flex-direction:column}}
</style>
